 value, or otherwise treat \\\"1.158\\\" and \\\"1.15800000\\\" as equivalent. AWS creates the Savings Plan, but Terraform fails the apply because the provider returns a different string value than the planned value. console Provider produced inconsistent result after apply .commitment: was cty.StringVal(\\\"1.158\\\"), but now cty\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-06-12T20:02:40Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.502,\n      \"band\": \"likely\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 46382,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#46382\",\n      \"title\": \"Importing `aws_savingsplans_savingsplan` resource triggers forced-replacement by `upfront_payment_amount` property\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"* aws_savingsplans_savings_plan upfront_payment_amount property cannot be configured by user. So this property shouldn't trigger forced-replacement It triggers forced-replacement console Click to expand configuration hcl # module.compute_savings_plan[\\\"compute-2025-07-21-3y-all-upfront\\\"].aws_savingsplans_savings_plan.this must be replaced -/+ resource \\\"aws_savingsplans_savings_plan\\\" \\\"this\\\" { ~ curr\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-09T13:42:31Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.386,\n      \"band\": \"possible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 46381,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#46381\",\n      \"title\": \"Importing `aws_savingsplans_savingsplan` resource is missing `savings_plan_offering_id` and `purchase_time`\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"* aws_savingsplans_savings_plan There should be no force-replacement with same savings_plan_offering_id and purchase_time of the Savings Plan. After importing the Savings plan, terraform always marked the resource for the force-replacement. console Click to expand configuration hcl # module.compute_savings_plan[\\\"compute-2025-07-21-3y-all-upfront\\\"].aws_savingsplans_savings_plan.this must be replace\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-09T13:39:15Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.359,\n      \"band\": \"possible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 46383,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#46383\",\n      \"title\": \"Support `aws_savingsplans_savings_plan_offering` and `aws_savingsplans_savings_plan_offerings` data source\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"To use aws_savingsplans_savings_plan resource, offering_id is required. The offering ID could be found using aws savingsplans describe-savings-plans-offerings CLI command or same API. The aws provider is already providing similar data sources for RDS / ElastiCache Reserved Instances. * data.aws_savingsplans_savings_plan_offering * data.aws_savingsplans_savings_plan_offerings hcl data \\\"aws_savingsp\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-09T13:53:24Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.311,\n      \"band\": \"possible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 47519,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#47519\",\n      \"title\": \"aws_savingsplans_savings_plan: Create times out when purchase_time is set to a future date (Queued state not treated as completion)\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"* aws_savingsplans_savings_plan When purchase_time is set to a future date, the Savings Plan is placed in queued state by the AWS API. This is the correct and final state until the scheduled purchase date arrives. The terraform apply should complete successfully, treating queued as a valid terminal state for scheduled purchases. terraform apply hangs during creation and eventually fails with a tim\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-04-18T17:40:01Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.19,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"corpus_size\": 11173,\n  \"thresholds\": {\n    \"likely\": 0.4,\n    \"possible\": 0.28\n  }\n}","is_erro