2026-10-28T17:39:26.6036333Z   
2026-10-28T17:39:26.6036971Z   - **Why a comment:** the reporter is on provider v6.42.0 and the latest release is v6.50.0, so the check marks the version as outdated. The comment asks them to confirm whether it still happens on v6.50.0. No release after v6.42.0 has a fix note for this resource, so it names none.
2026-10-28T17:39:26.6038206Z   - **Why not a duplicate:** I compared the similar issues the duplicate search returned. #48393 is about the `commitment` value being normalized, and #46382 is about `upfront_payment_amount` forcing replacement on import. Neither is the same problem as `upfront_payment_amount` changing from null to `"0.00000000"` after create.
2026-10-28T17:39:26.6039297Z   - **Labels:** the issue already has `bug` from its form, and the regex labeler will add `service/savingsplans`. `waiting-response` was the only label left to add.
